{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Less_computation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Less computation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Easy_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Easy Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A right pyramid has regular octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as its base and apex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0370c751a4b0f88b2c9b6a364f304ad9258d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> Segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adcc6d5d636a7a75e6c391b31694cbbd8010340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a133680e8095a20d79f20ca80fe7b073fa87e51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> are perpendicular. What is the square of the height of the pyramid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a3c8cdf80f62d88185a2aa6a928b28ea757d30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1+\\sqrt2}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\sqrt2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac32 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{2+\\sqrt2}{3} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"508\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the height of the pyramid, we need the length from the center of the octagon (denote as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) to its vertices and the length of AV. \n</p><p>From symmetry, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957612224a46cd63154fa1b201358f8231c0411e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AV} = \\overline{DV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4b9a2a3c18a981be2006c13c7581b621d1d861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AVD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adcc6d5d636a7a75e6c391b31694cbbd8010340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/14813e31bf2a27561a9d5b7038aeda2525cbe224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD} = x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"21\" />. Dropping the altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> in isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> (we know this from the fact that it is a regular octagon) reveals that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fefaf5074909b695b8f8ceeeb3ce1113faa6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}=1+2(\\sqrt{2}/2)=1+\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"232\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bcbd0891337b14b1b43ea74096cec34a998c6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AV}=(\\overline{AD})/\\sqrt{2}=(\\sqrt{2}+2)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"243\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p>To find the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f70416d14a373677c13bb4a45d204e5229a1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IA$\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" />, we cut the octagon into 8 triangles, each with a smallest angle of 45 degrees. Using the law of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6454bcefc01151e2d6d5858df8883eb1fee310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AIB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> reveals that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/55882d18099f0fef63c0d3ce97cedd7fa1697905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IA^2=(2+\\sqrt{2})/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p>Finally, using the Pythagorean theorem, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f0a6b84f8b5586e8045b654f4f06d8733a0ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\overline{IV}}^2={\\overline{AV}}^2-{\\overline{IA}}^2= {((2+\\sqrt{2})/2)}^2 - (2+\\sqrt{2})/2 = \\boxed{(1+\\sqrt{2})/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"513\" height=\"35\" /> which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>～username2333\n~hashbrown2009\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Less_computation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Less_computation)\">Solution 2 (Less computation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Less computation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the regular octagon. Connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. It is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266a950fe810cf50be081df605ed5c47b0360568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VI=\\frac{1}{2} AD=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b673115d76f4430e75321009be1ac7b96850abe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI=\\frac{1}{2}AH=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />. Hence, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/24116157b4666d1f5da1196562d61027b6caee76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[VO^2=VI^2-OI^2\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b490ca580ed476fcbb9b1635842223a3ff78259d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left(\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{1}{4}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"57\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3ad3ad7dbbaf101d7bc5d8d46ce3577608b11a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"41\" /> \nHence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~tsun26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c7/2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg/600px-2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"849\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c7/2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg/900px-2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c7/2024_AMC_12B_P23.jpeg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>~Kathan\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Easy_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Easy_Geometry)\">Solution 4 (Easy Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Easy Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_12B_2024_Problem23.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"None\"><img alt=\"None\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/f/f7/AMC_12B_2024_Problem23.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"398\" height=\"502\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Firstly, scale each of the sides up by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71df1b44d6caa4b0f798d48ff8ee72da386e4cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, and split the octagon into half. Next, divide the octagon into a rectangle and the isosceles trapezoid, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the points where the shapes coincide. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the rectangle (which is also the center of the octagon.) By drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangles in the trapezoid, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feec7855ed8a7de72c5a121e631c07b8a957bc5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 4+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />. Now, consider the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. It is half of the diagonal of the rectangle, and since the diagonal is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d07b65e0d7bdebbbc80838c2481d2329382ca31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(4+2\\sqrt{2})^{2}} = \\sqrt{8+24+16\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{32+16\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"464\" height=\"36\" />, the length of AI is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d9638d2a221d30be2bff37490625e493e2b8581f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{8+4\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"84\" height=\"35\" />. Now, consider triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a34c4051b2092e8a22855e1f5737f2f18b028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. The apex of a regular pyramid is defined to be equidistant from every vertex, and since segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7478949eb3c36f58ef0d04b3fb861a0451a56c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8dafdc57cd66768e961faccbb1ed2853edb893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular, then triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a34c4051b2092e8a22855e1f5737f2f18b028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> right triangle with the right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. This means that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7478949eb3c36f58ef0d04b3fb861a0451a56c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8dafdc57cd66768e961faccbb1ed2853edb893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/732d9762c14aa974ea242324988f74f84c7a645d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{4+2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = 2\\sqrt{2} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"217\" height=\"48\" />. Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20be3b677019ce41db8143a9a892e80a8a8f9f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AIV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle. Applying Pythagorean Theorem yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911d167011e25e1d009f70d6b11a52e9fa8a4e5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV^{2} = (2\\sqrt{2} + 2)^{2} - (8+4\\sqrt{2}) = 4+4\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"334\" height=\"24\" />. However, initially we had scaled each of the sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71df1b44d6caa4b0f798d48ff8ee72da386e4cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so we have to divide the answer by the square of that, so the real answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148930629ed95330290f70a564cbbcd4ab376a55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore the answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc55ddcfa3f7733d21d98dfc20d01cca8b8657be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1+\\sqrt2}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"107\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>~mathwizard123123\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Vectors)\">Solution 5 (Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cbee0447a6e7c5d6dbfe3aadfc0d37d4fb939e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{AV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad068dd33ea17f4352cb0951a0323efbfc4313ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{DV}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" />.\nIf we use a coordinate plane where one of the axes is parallel to one of the sides of the octagon, we can calculate each of the vectors to be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525911269d492cfbc7a54831b7aa6caaece1ef55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\vec{AV} = \\left\\langle \\frac{1}{2},  \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}, h \\right\\rangle\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e007b2656164412dbaedc7a7c6f5ae547a4e7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\vec{DV} = \\left\\langle \\frac{1}{2},  \\frac{-1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}, h \\right\\rangle\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"53\" />\nNow, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae2d402a50a42cc0582d05d3ddd1b5ef2986a49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{AV} \\cdot \\vec{DV} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> if the vectors are perpendicular to each other, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf9b248c24250b2f1e60e53172796b36aac508c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{2},  \\frac{-1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}, h \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\left\\langle \\frac{1}{2},  \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}, h \\right\\rangle = \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{3 + 2\\sqrt{2}}{4} + h^2 = 0\\]\" width=\"482\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc2a54c6c9906dd4ae8f788d023ee6b27a21506.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h^2=\\frac{2+2\\sqrt{2}}{4}=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Yielding answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~tkl\n</p><p>==Only B and D looks normal , guess one using掐头去尾\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-PzTyKqqV4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G-PzTyKqqV4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p